Checkpoint reload -- two processes, one research state
======================================================

The snapshot is removed before session one and kept for session two.
Session two is a fresh process: taught rules are recompiled from their
checkpointed formal terms before use, and request indices are stable.

----- session one (cold) -----

you> research mode on
hyge> research mode ON. Derivation-cache answers, comparison shortcuts, prewritten ladders and target-specific schemata are not available here: this runtime holds only live-taught knowledge. Residual states are preserved. `audit knowledge` now prints the cold-start manifest.

you> assume axiom: (rel a b)
hyge> axiom recorded with provenance DOMAIN_AXIOM: (rel a b)

you> teach law: (rule (premises (rel ?x ?y) (mark ?y)) (conclusion (tag ?x)))
hyge> taught and compiled with provenance HUMAN_SUPPLIED_TRUSTED_THEOREM: (rule ((rel ?x ?y) (mark ?y)) (tag ?x))
note: teaching stores knowledge; it demonstrates nothing until a retry or counterfactual measures progress.

you> attempt goal: (tag a)
hyge> FAILED. cost=1; attempted operational rules with a genuine partial match: 1
the root remains in the residual record even with zero successors; `suggest dependencies` compiles requests only from concrete unmatched premises.

you> suggest dependencies
hyge> dependency requests from attempted rules:
  [0] status=ObservedMissingPremise kind=THEOREM need=(Need (mark b))

you> approve dependency 0
hyge> approved dependency [0] status=SpeculativeDependency
note: approval is a hypothesis, not evidence. Usefulness is demonstrated only by measured counterfactual unlock.

you> goodbye
hyge> goodbye

----- session two (restored from checkpoint) -----

you> research mode on
hyge> restoring the research checkpoint (taught rules will be recompiled and revalidated)
hyge> research mode ON. Derivation-cache answers, comparison shortcuts, prewritten ladders and target-specific schemata are not available here: this runtime holds only live-taught knowledge. Residual states are preserved. `audit knowledge` now prints the cold-start manifest.

you> audit knowledge
hyge> audit knowledge (research runtime -- live-taught knowledge only):
  [0] HUMAN_SUPPLIED_TRUSTED_THEOREM: (rule ((rel ?x ?y) (mark ?y)) (tag ?x))
  [1] DOMAIN_AXIOM: (rel a b)
  intervention episodes: 0
  learned policies: none

you> show dependencies
hyge> dependency requests (all):
  [0] status=SpeculativeDependency kind=THEOREM need=(Need (mark b))

you> attempt goal: (tag a)
hyge> FAILED. cost=1; attempted operational rules with a genuine partial match: 1
the root remains in the residual record even with zero successors; `suggest dependencies` compiles requests only from concrete unmatched premises.

you> teach dependency 0: (rule (premises (rel ?u ?v)) (conclusion (mark ?v)))
hyge> counterfactual fork measured a real unlock: cost 1 -> 2; newly enabled existing firings: 1; goal closed: yes
status=DemonstratedUsefulDependency; intervention episode recorded; `retry parent goal` to apply it for real.

you> retry parent goal
hyge> retry: goal closed

you> show intervention episodes
hyge> intervention episodes (newest first):
[0] residual=(mark b) outcome=DemonstratedUsefulDependency

you> goodbye
hyge> goodbye
